From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Isuru Fernando <ifernando@openteams.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the abseil systemlib work with conda-forge libabseil

Squash of the feedstock's abseil systemlib patches:

- Restore the system_build_file/system_link_files wiring for abseil that
  TF 2.21.0 dropped (re-add SYS_DIRS, incl. the crc and log dirs), so the
  system.absl.*.BUILD files are used with TF_SYSTEM_LIBS=com_google_absl.
- Declare targets referenced by TF/XLA but missing from the systemlib
  BUILD files: log (log, check, die_if_null, vlog_is_on, globals, flags,
  initialize, log_entry, log_sink, ...), crc (crc32c and internals),
  strings:string_view, base:nullability/prefetch/tracing_internal/
  no_destructor, synchronization:kernel_timeout_internal,
  container:hash_container_defaults, functional:overload,
  hash:hash_testing, status:status_matchers.
- Fix linkopts for the current libabseil library layout: absl_log_flags
  instead of absl_flags, vlog_config_internal, drop absl_low_level_hash
  (merged into absl_hash in 20260107) and libraries removed from
  random/types, and add missing abseil linkages.
- batching_util: depend on base:tracing_internal.

Co-authored-by: Uwe L. Korn <uwe.korn@quantco.com>
Co-authored-by: H. Vetinari <h.vetinari@gmx.com>
Co-authored-by: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: Filippo Luca Ferretti <filippoluca.ferretti@outlook.com>
---
